{"status": "VERIFIED_ALL_DIMENSION_CONSTANT_CUT_BUDGET_AND_EXACT_CYCLE_REPAIR", "core_theorem": "For k>=4, v_k=(16*2^(k-5),...,16,1,6,8,4) has D=0,K=2, phi=2^(k-2)-2, R_min=2^(k-2)+1.", "high_theorem": "For n>=5, append H=1+sum(v_(n-1)). Then D=0,K=4,lambda=1, phi=2^(n-2)-3, R_min=2^(n-2)+2.", "scope": "No positive-density D+K-only or D+K+lambda-only inequality can hold uniformly over genuine generic scans. The main M_n and universal paired quarter problems remain open.", "violations": 0, "seconds": 1.6772213429940166, "audit_sha256": "801de14ec9409a97751d2534ff5341cbe92d295b143b697c94b86934b7177729"}
